# Helm templates contain Go template syntax that Prettier doesn't understand
**/templates/**

# CRD manifests are auto-generated by controller-gen and should not be reformatted
**/crds/**

# Minified/bundled assets should not be reformatted
**/dist/

# Generated public docs manifest: a build output of
# //projects/monolith/frontend:docs_manifest (#6446), gitignored where the
# generator writes a local copy for `pnpm dev`. The generator is the sole
# authority for its layout.
**/docs-manifest.json

# Generated ADR 036 orchestrator context bundle: produced deterministically by
# projects/monolith/knowledge/tools/gen_orchestrator_bundle.py and used as the
# byte-stable system prefix for provider prompt caching. Prettier would re-add
# blank lines before the digest lists and race the generator; the generator is
# the sole authority (same rationale as docs-manifest.json above).
**/chat/orchestrator_bundle.md

# STPA fragments and rendered output are deterministically produced by the jq
# renderer in docs/agents/stpa.md. Reformatting would diverge from the renderer
# output and churn on every scheduled regeneration; the renderer is the sole
# authority.
**/STPA.md
**/stpa/*.json

# Git worktrees have their own formatting
.claude/worktrees/

# Prose (Markdown) and YAML: Prettier owns CODE, not prose. The CI formatter
# (//bazel/tools/format:format_code) wires prettier to the `javascript` language
# slot ONLY, so CI never reformats .md or .yaml. Local ci lint also selects
# changed Markdown and YAML files. Ignoring these here scopes local prettier
# to match CI: prose is hand-written (see the repo's no-em-dash / minimal-churn
# rules) and no CI check enforces its formatting. The specific generated .md/.json
# entries above are kept as documentation of why those particular files are
# generator-owned, even though this blanket rule now also covers the .md ones.
**/*.md
**/*.yaml
**/*.yml

# Session collector fixtures are JSON Lines (one JSON object per line), which
# Prettier has no parser for; they are hand-written test inputs, not code.
tools/session_collector/fixtures/*.jsonl
# Muse 1.4.1 exec fixture is a verbatim two-turn JSONL recording from the
# pinned CLI (same rationale as above): byte-stable test input, not code.
projects/embervm/runtimes/claude/muse_exec_echo_two_turns_1_4_1.jsonl
